                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is a top-down arcadey shooter where you use crates with power weapons and your character's special move to kill spawning varieties of zombies and martians (only in the third campaign chapter or survival). \n\nIt has a campaign mode, a survival mode, and a time trials mode. Campaign is three chapters of three missions. Each mission is broken into objectives that include standing in a circle for an amount of time, taking a cheerleader to a place, killing an amount of specific enemies, defending a cheerleader or machine, or blowing up a machine. None of them are all that fun or interesting. Survival is just an endless horde mode. Time trials is just survival but timed. \n\nI hate to speak ill of a small studio doing their best, but the game is just mediocre. You play the first mission, and you've seen most of what the game has to offer. You can, probably, beat the campaign missions in an hour. Two, at most. I know shouldn't expect the world from a $5 game, and it's not like nobody would ever have fun with it, but there just really isn't anything to recommend here.\n\nOh, and I try not to talk about achievements in reviews because not everyone cares about them, and I don't think they should be make or break, but look at my play time. That is ALL because of achievements. They are FAR too grindy, and I still have several hours to go.",
